From 4d8afd6e122fe5435f263eb2cf5ffa7b41d9d3dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cheol Ho Choi <cheolho.choi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 03:27:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] feat: MRSF low-rank J/K fast path through the Route-C bridge
 (APIV2.1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

mrsfcbc optionally captures the rank-1/rank-2 factor vectors of d3 slots
1-6 (the tmp intermediates it forms anyway; dense build untouched) into a
parallel (nbf,8,nvec) array; tdhf_mrsf_energy threads it to the consumer
as int2_mrsf_data_t%d3fac. int2_routec routes slots 1-4 (rank-1) and 5-6
(rank-2) through the new optional dylib symbol routec_jkm_apply_lr
(K(uv^T) = sum_P (B_P u)(B_P v)^T — no nbf^3 term; ~nbf/2x fewer FLOPs on
6 of 7 slots), slot 7 stays dense. Dense branch kept 100% intact as
fallback and referee; OQP_ROUTEC_LR=0 forces it.

Gates (this Mac, exact-Cholesky B, H2O/6-31G* MRSF BHHLYP S+T):
lr-injected vs dense-injected excitations <= 7e-16 Ha (gate 1e-10);
engine lr vs dense K 4.6e-14 abs; lr K-orientation tripwire 7.5e0.
Z-vector/UMRSF paths unchanged (d3fac stays null there => dense).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
